## 2. Deadline: September 30, 2026 — Container Image Vulnerabilities

**Applies to:** apps with RTO ≤ 744 hours (newly in scope)
**Requirement [TECH06.03]:** No critical/high vulnerabilities with known exploits in production container images.

- [ ] Identify which apps in the inventory fall into the ≤744h tier for the first time
- [ ] Run/check current vulnerability scan results for those apps
- [ ] Triage and remediate critical/high findings with known exploits
- [ ] Confirm remediation status in the **PtO Insights Platform**
- [ ] Re-scan and verify clean before Sept 30, 2026

---

## 3. Already-Enforced NFRs (RTO ≤ 72 hours)

For each app already in this tier, confirm:

- [ ] **Authorized Change Implementor** — prod deploys initiated by the ServiceNow-assigned implementor or an authorized service account
- [ ] **Artifact Attribution** — ServiceNow change record identifies the deployed artifact
- [ ] **Least Privilege** — deployment platform access is least-privilege and periodically reviewed
- [ ] **Enterprise Customer MFA** — customer-facing apps enforce MFA [TECH09.13]
- [ ] **Enterprise Tooling MFA** — deployment tooling enforces MFA for authorized users
- [ ] **Enterprise Pipeline Tooling** — deploys run through GitHub Actions / XLR / ISPW
- [ ] **Enterprise Platform Tooling** — deploys target approved hosting (Cloud, Mainframe, TIMS, etc.)
- [ ] **Enterprise Artifact Tooling** — built artifacts stored in Artifactory
- [ ] **Enterprise Version Control Tooling** — source resides in GitHub/ISPW
- [ ] **Lower Environment Validation** — lower-env deploy/validation completed before prod
- [ ] **Implementation Strategy Verification** — documented implementation strategy on the change record
- [ ] **Validation Strategy Verification** — documented, executable validation steps on the change record

